	<templatedescription>Roborock vacuum status and control through a LAN HTTP bridge, with a Navigator web view (state, battery, Start / Pause / Dock / Stop) and state-based tile icons. UNTESTED.</templatedescription>

	<!--
		v5 (0.5.0) - Active Room and Room Progress properties; web page vacuum2.html, build 3 (UNTESTED on hardware and in Composer)
		v2 (0.2.0) - uibutton proxy and Navigator web view (UNTESTED on hardware and in Composer)
		The uibutton proxy on binding 5001 opens www/vacuum2.html. The page reads the UI_STATE snapshot
		and sends UI_START / UI_PAUSE / UI_DOCK / UI_STOP through ExecuteCommand. The tile icon changes
		with state: Default, Cleaning, Docked (docked or charging), Error.
		Changing the proxy means the device must be deleted and re-added in Composer.
		PACKAGE NAME: roborock.c4z. <name> is the same slug so controller://driver/roborock/... resolves.
		PAGE FILE IS RENAMED EVERY PAGE RELEASE (vacuum1, vacuum2, ...). web_view_url, PAGE_BUILD / UI_BUILD
		in the Lua and the file in www/ must agree.
		Commands, actions, events, variables and properties from v1 are unchanged.
		v5.1 (0.5.1) - events moved to devicedata level so Composer lists them
		v5.2 (0.6.0) - Room field shows Docked when docked or charging and the target room (e.g. "Laundry (target)") while a room job runs; events 8 Laundry Room Clean Started and 9 Laundry Room Clean Finished (UNTESTED on hardware and in Composer)
		v5.3 (0.6.2) - Laundry Room Clean Started fires as soon as the bridge accepts a clean job that includes the Laundry Room ID; adaptive polling (5 s while cleaning, Poll Interval otherwise; default 15, minimum 5) (UNTESTED on hardware and in Composer)
	-->
	<events>
		<event>
			<id>1</id>
			<name>Cleaning Started</name>
			<description>Fires when the vacuum enters a cleaning state</description>
		</event>
		<event>
			<id>2</id>
			<name>Cleaning Finished</name>
			<description>Fires when cleaning ends and the vacuum returns to docked or charging</description>
		</event>
		<event>
			<id>3</id>
			<name>Error Raised</name>
			<description>Fires when the bridge reports a new vacuum error</description>
		</event>
		<event>
			<id>4</id>
			<name>Battery Low</name>
			<description>Fires when battery is at or below Low Battery Threshold (once until it recovers)</description>
		</event>
		<event>
			<id>5</id>
			<name>Bridge Unreachable</name>
			<description>Fires when the LAN bridge cannot be reached or returns an error</description>
		</event>
		<event>
			<id>6</id>
			<name>Laundry Room Entered</name>
			<description>Fires when the robot is in the Laundry Room ID while cleaning (uses the bridge's current room). Falls back to cleaning start on a laundry-only run when the current room is unknown</description>
		</event>
		<event>
			<id>7</id>
			<name>Laundry Room Left</name>
			<description>Fires when the robot leaves the Laundry Room ID while cleaning, or when cleaning ends (docked, charging or idle; not on pause)</description>
		</event>
		<event>
			<id>8</id>
			<name>Laundry Room Clean Started</name>
			<description>Fires when a clean job that includes the Laundry Room ID starts (from the driver's Clean Rooms action or web view). Does not depend on the robot's current room, so it fires while the robot travels to the laundry</description>
		</event>
		<event>
			<id>9</id>
			<name>Laundry Room Clean Finished</name>
			<description>Fires when a clean job that included the Laundry Room ID ends (docked, charging or idle; not on pause)</description>
		</event>
	</events>
	<config>
		<power_management_method>AlwaysOn</power_management_method>
		<power_command_delay>0</power_command_delay>
		<power_delay>0</power_delay>
		<power_command_needed>False</power_command_needed>
